cing and transporting crude oil and natural gas; processing, liquefaction, transportation and regasification associated with liquefied natural gas; transporting crude oil by major international oil export pipelines; transporting, storage and marketing of natural gas; carbon capture and storage; and a gas-to-liquids plant. Downstream operations consist primarily of refining crude oil into petroleum products; marketing of crude oil, refined products and lubricants; manufacturing and marketing of renewable fuels; transporting crude oil and refined pro","zh":"Chevron？ developing, producing and transporting crude oil and natural gas; processing, liquefaction, transportation and regasification associated with liquefied natural gas; transporting crude oil by major international oil export pipelines transporting crude oil by major international oil export pipelines; Downstream operations consist primarily of refining crude oil into petroleum products; marketing of crude oil, refined products and lubricants;可再生燃料的製造和營銷；運輸原油和成品油"},{"en":"Petroleum industry operations and profitability are influenced by many factors. Prices for crude oil, natural gas, liquefied natural gas (LNG), petroleum products and petrochemicals are generally determined by supply and demand. Production levels from the members of Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC), Russia and the United States are major factors in determining worldwide supply. Demand for crude oil and its products and for natural gas is largely driven by the conditions of local, national and global economies, although weather patterns, the pace of energy transition and taxation relative to other energy sources also play a significant part. Laws and governmental policies, particularly in the areas of taxation, energy and the environment, affect where and how companies invest, conduct their operations, select feedstocks, and formulate their products and, in some cases,","zh":"石油業的營運和獲利能力受到多種因素的影響。 Prices for crude oil, natural gas, liquefied natural gas (LNG), petroleum products and petrochemicals are generally determined by supply and demand. Production levels from the members of Organization of Unitediation Countlet. determining worldwide supply. Demand for crude oil and its products and for natural gas is largely driven by the conditions of local, national and global economies, although weather patterns, the pace of energy transst and taxation relgy andalification relgy caters play cat ​​yleative and catgy relative catulity catulity catulity catululation catululation signululation signal catulity catulity catulstinsulations catulity 體育面 體育面 格式。 governmental policies, particularly in the areas of taxation, energy and the environment, affect where and how companies invest, conduct their operations, select feedstocks, and formulate their products and, in some cases,"},{"en":"Strong competition exists in all sectors of the petroleum and petrochemical industries in supplying the energy, fuel and chemical needs of industry and individual consumers. In the upstream business, Chevron competes with fully integrated, major global petroleum companies, as well as independent and national petroleum companies, for the acquisition of crude oil and natural gas leases and other properties and for the equipment and labor required to develop and operate those properties. In its downstream business, Chevron competes with fully integrated, major petroleum companies, as well as independent refining and marketing, transportation and chemicals entities and national petroleum companies in the refining, manufacturing, sale and marketing of fuels, lubricants, additives and petrochemicals.","zh":""}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Chevron holds an approximately 38 percent consolidated ownership interest in Hess Midstream LP (HESM) following the acquisition of Hess. HESM provides fee-based services for Chevron and third-party customers in the Bakken. The midstream integrated infrastructure is primarily located in McKenzie, Williams, and Mountrail Counties, North Dakota, and Mentor, Minnesota. It includes a natural gas gathering and compression system, a crude oil gathering system and a produced water gathering and disposal system. Key facilities include the Tioga Gas Plant, 50 percent ownership of the Little Missouri 4 gas plant, the Mentor Propane Storage Terminal, the Ramberg Terminal crude oil facility, the Tioga Rail Terminal and a fleet of 550 crude oil rail cars. Additional infrastructure such as the Johnson's Corner Header System and various connections to the Dakota Access Pipeline provide further crude oil","zh":"收購 Hess 後，雪佛龍持有 Hess Midstream LP (HESM) 約 38% 的合併所有權權益。 HESM 為巴肯的雪佛龍和第三方客戶提供收費服務。中游綜合基礎設施主要位於北達科他州的麥肯齊縣、威廉斯縣和蒙特雷爾縣以及明尼蘇達州的門託縣。它包括天然氣收集和壓縮系統、原油收集系統和採出水收集和處理系統。 Key facilities include the Tioga Gas Plant, 50 percent ownership of the Little Missouri 4 gas plant, the Mentor Propane Storage Terminal, the Ramberg Terminal crude oil facility, the Tioga Rail Terminal and a structeet of 550 crude oil rail cars. various connections to the Dakota Access Pipeline provide further crude oil"}],"competition":[],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2025-12-31","items":[{"name":"Reportable Segment Aggregation Before Other Operating","val":230789000000,"zh":"其他經營分部之前的可報告分部總結"},{"name":"All Other Segments","val":644000000,"zh":"所有其他部門"}],"total":189031000000}},"peers":["XOM","COP","JNJ","PG","OXY"]}}